+    page-aligned offsets from 0, and padding fills the rest out to the bucket,
+    which is `max_running_requests` times the page-aligned `max_req_len`. A pass
+    over the whole bucket builds `[tokens, heads, bucket]` logits and
+    `[tokens, bucket]` masks in every layer: Inkling's check launch on a v5p-64
+    has a 5,329,408-slot bucket and asks for 1.43 TB of temporaries per chip.
+    This loop visits only the blocks that hold the batch's slots and carries an
+    online softmax across them, so it holds one tile at a time and reads each
+    request's KV and nothing past it, the way the FA backend's pages do.
+
+    `position_bias` is `[tokens, heads, extent]`, one bias per backward
+    distance. A distance at or past the extent adds zero. The softmax runs in
+    float32. A padding row sees no key and comes out zero.
